<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    HSK patch: gate VFE Insectoids 2 raids on the vanilla Insect faction
    behind a minimum raid-points threshold so they don't appear in
    early-game / low-wealth / tribal scenarios.

    Why?
    Same problem as the Junker pirates: Megascarabs (combatPower ~30)
    are cheap enough that the storyteller can pack a few into a 200-400
    point early raid budget against a tribal start. Result: day-4
    Norbal colony gets swarmed by hive insects.

    Fix: the Combat pawnGroupMaker that VFE Insectoids 2 adds to the
    vanilla Insect faction gets <minTotalPoints>800</minTotalPoints>.
    Below 800 points the storyteller can't pick this group as a raid
    source. At higher wealth insect raids kick in normally.

    Note: VFE I2's raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve already starts at
    (300, 0) → (700, 1), so insect raids were already de-weighted at
    low points — but the curve only changes commonality, not eligibility.
    A minTotalPoints gate is a hard floor.

    Settlement pawnGroupMakers are NOT gated — they govern base
    composition, not raid eligibility.

    Targets the Combat pawnGroupMaker via kindDef="Combat" xpath selector.
-->
<Patch>

    <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="Insect"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"]</xpath>
        <value>
            <minTotalPoints>800</minTotalPoints>
        </value>
    </Operation>

</Patch>
